# Comparison

| Approach       | Time | Space | Idea                                                          |
| -------------- | ---- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Brute Force    | O(n) | O(1)  | Generate odd/even numbers, compute sums, then GCD             |
| Optimal (Math) | O(1) | O(1)  | Use formulas: `sumOdd = n²`, `sumEven = n(n+1)`, so `GCD = n` |

### Key Pattern to Remember

* Sum of first `n` odd numbers = `n²`
* Sum of first `n` even numbers = `n(n+1)`
* `gcd(n, n+1) = 1` (consecutive integers are always coprime)
* Therefore, `gcd(n², n(n+1)) = n`
